<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shangjing of Liao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">918–1120</span> · Also known as Liao Supreme Capital, Liao Shangjing, Linhuang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shangjing, the Supreme Capital, was the principal capital of the Khitan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-liao">Abaoji</a> in 918 in present-day Bairin Left Banner, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-mongolia">Inner Mongolia</a>. It had a northern city for the Khitan court and a southern city for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-chinese">Han Chinese</a> and other subjects. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> Jin captured it in 1120 during their conquest of the Liao, and its walls and foundations survive as an archaeological site.</p></div>
